  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `MoveModel` (and so `LocatePart`) keeps the stock's own rotation when the move does not turn the part. Before, the float noise of the locate solve (about 5e-14) became a stored stock rotation, and the stock sim refused the stock in a vise.\n- `stock_follow::sim_frame` is the one law for the stock frame of the simulation. `stock_sim::stock_grid`, `stock_sim_held::first_body` / `first_field` and `stock_view::stock_facets` read it.\n  - An unturned stock is unchanged.\n  - A box turned by a quarter-turn multiple (within 1e-9) is its unturned twin with the sides swapped.\n  - An upright cylinder is an unturned cylinder.\n  - A from-model stock is read from its placed mesh at any turn.\n  - An oblique box and a laid cylinder are refused by name (`OBLIQUE_STOCK`, `LAID_CYLINDER`).\n- The UI says a simulation refusal one time, in plain words. The uncut stock stays drawn.\n- Review fix (commit 465638b09): four suites used a stock turned a quarter about Z to make the program sim refuse. The device is now a turn of 1e-6 rad about Z (`OBLIQUE`), which the sim refuses by name. See \"Readings\".\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2177-square-stock-sim.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nEffect: a project whose stock had locate noise or a quarter turn was \"not judged\" by the stock sim. Now the sim judges it, and a gouge that the sim finds can block the post. No posted G-code changes. No golden `.nc` / `.cl` file and no snapshot PNG changes.\n\nThe review found 9 red tests. In each case the PR is correct and the test device was wrong:\n\n| Test (suite) | Reading |\n|---|---|\n| `deep-Engrave-true`, `low-top-Engrave-true`, `wall-Engrave-true` (`engrave_law`) | The cut is a real gouge (the operation convicts it too). The post was refused. The sim now judges the quarter-turned stock, so its gouge clause leads the message. |\n| `through` and `stock-through` / `stock-web` Engrave (`mark_floor` lines 160, 253) | Same: a cut through the 2 mm plate. The sim convicts it correctly. |\n| `into-a-trace-true` (`neighbour_law`) | Same: the flank enters part A by 0.3 mm. The sim finds 0.3 mm on A, as on the aligned stock. |\n| `low-stock-face-true`, `slot-false-true`, `engrave-false-true` (`stock_source_law`) | Same: cuts off the stock into the part. |\n\nThe `by_op` checks are kept and are not loosened. They pin that the operation's own gouge blocks the post when the sim does not judge. Each `by_op` check now also asserts that the sim refuses the stock with `OBLIQUE_STOCK`, so the device cannot become silent. The fixture box check takes 1e-4 mm in X and Y for the 1e-6 rad turn (the corners move by less than 6e-5 mm). Z stays at 1e-9.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `stock_in_vise_sim` (2 tests): a located stock in a vise is simulated; an oblique stock is refused by name.\n- New, one in each suite: `a_quarter_turned_stock_is_judged_by_the_program_sim` in `engrave_law`, `mark_floor`, `neighbour_law`, `stock_source_law`. The quarter-turned stock is judged, its gouge blocks the post, and a legal mark posts.\n- The MCP parity test of `stock_source_law` moved to the new suite `stock_source_law_mcp` (the 400-line law). The `#[test]` count grows by 4: 28 to 32 in the five suites.\n\n## Gate (on the PR head, not merged with main)\n\n- `engrave_law` 10/10, `mark_floor` 7/7, `neighbour_law` 7/7, `stock_source_law` 7/7, `stock_source_law_mcp` 1/1.\n- `stock_in_vise_sim` 2/2, `post_not_judged` 4/4, `area_controls` 13/13, `pocket_recognition` 11/11 (they share the changed test modules).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -j 6 -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The review run (trial merge with main `1f15f98e7`) covers the rest: app lib 353, ui lib 949 and 13 ui suites, `stock_sim_document`, `stock_view`, `rotary_field_parity`, `posting`, `verify`, `stock_source_verdict`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real control or machine.\n- No GUI run for this fix.\n- Not built merged with the current `main`: the PR merges cleanly, and the current `main` has a debug build error in work by a different agent.\n- The combination with PR #2184 (`fixture_locate_stock`, `fixture_locate_stock_body`, `stock_in_vise_sim`) is not run. Run them after the second of the two merges.\n\nChangelog: The simulation now shows and judges a stock held in a vise after a locate, and a stock turned by a quarter turn; a stock turned off the machine axes is refused in plain words.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2177\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
